<header class="sg-head"><p class="featured-region">Anthem · 1952 · Egypt &amp; North Africa</p><h1 class="sg-title">Cherifian Anthem</h1><p class="sg-local"><bdi lang="ar" dir="rtl">النشيد الشريف</bdi> / <bdi lang="ar-Latn">an-našīd aš-šarīf</bdi></p><p class="sg-kid" data-say>The national anthem of Morocco. Its tune was written in the 1950s, and its words were added in 1970.</p></header>
<dl class="sg-facts"><div><dt>Words</dt><dd>Ali Squalli Houssaini</dd></div><div><dt>Music</dt><dd>Léo Morgan</dd></div><div><dt>Culture</dt><dd>Morocco</dd></div><div><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd></div><div><dt>Place</dt><dd>Morocco</dd></div><div><dt>Date</dt><dd>melody believed composed in 1952; words adopted in 1970</dd></div><div><dt>Type</dt><dd>Anthem</dd></div><div><dt>The words</dt><dd>In copyright (words by Ali Squalli Houssaini, adopted 1970 (melody by Léo Morgan, believed composed 1952))</dd></div></dl>
<div class="sg-body">
<section class="sg-sec" id="story"><h2>The story</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cherifian-anthem">Cherifian Anthem</a> is the national anthem of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>. Its melody was composed by Léo Morgan, a French military officer who was chief of music for the Moroccan Royal Guard, during the French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a>. It is believed to have been composed in 1952, four years before Morocco's independence in 1956, and the anthem has been in use since the protectorate period.</p><p>The words came later. After the Moroccan national football team qualified for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fifa-world-cup">FIFA World Cup</a> for the first time, for the 1970 tournament, the idea of writing lyrics for the anthem was proposed. The lyrics were written by the Moroccan author and poet Professor Ali Squalli Houssaini and adopted in 1970. Accounts differ on how they were chosen: either King Hassan II picked them in a competition, or he commissioned Squalli Houssaini to write them directly.</p></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="meaning"><h2>What it says</h2><p>A national anthem of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>, sung on state occasions.</p></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="words"><h2>The words</h2><p class="sg-nowords" data-say>The words of this song are still in copyright, so they are not printed here. &#8220;What it says&#8221; above gives their theme in our own words, and the performance below lets you hear them.</p></section>
